        "comments": "The assembly lpElePalu1.hap1.1 is based on 77x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. It looks like the species could have been dodecaploid, based on the faded similarity lines on the haploid HiC map and today it works as a tetraploid (4n = 38). Each haplotype file has two copies of each set of 4 chromosomes, evenly distributed in HAP1 and HAP2 files (19 chromosomes in each). A translocation was observed between Chromosome 1 339.35 Mbp - 457.90 Mbp and the entire Chromosome 18, reason why the total number of chromosomes is not a multiple of 4. Some haplotypic inversions were detected on: Chromosome 2 271.31 Mbp - 274.99 Mbp, Chromosome 2 331.92 Mbp - 348.88 Mbp, Chromosome 3 20.56 Mbp - 45.46 Mbp, Chromosome 4 95.39 Mbp - 98.57 Mbp and Chromosome 12 109.03 Mbp - 133.06 Mbp.",
